# Theme Hooks

Use the theme hooks from `@/lib/theme/hooks` and `@/lib/theme/context` for all theme-aware styling. Never hardcode color values.

## When to Use Each Hook

### `useThemeColor()` - For Raw Color Values

Use when you need an actual hex color value (e.g., icon `color` props, chart colors, or any component API that requires a color string):

```tsx
import { useThemeColor } from "@/lib/theme/hooks";

const getThemeColor = useThemeColor();
const iconColor = getThemeColor("foreground");
const destructiveColor = getThemeColor("destructive");

<Icon color={iconColor} />;
```

Available color names: `background`, `foreground`, `card`, `card-foreground`, `primary`, `primary-foreground`, `secondary`, `secondary-foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `accent`, `accent-foreground`, `success`, `destructive`, `destructive-foreground`, `border`, `input`, `ring`, `chart`.

### `useThemeColorClassName()` - For NativeWind Classes

Use when applying Tailwind/NativeWind class names that need theme awareness:

```tsx
import { useThemeColorClassName } from "@/lib/theme/hooks";

const getThemeColor = useThemeColorClassName();

<View className={getThemeColor("bg-background")} />
<Text className={getThemeColor("text-foreground")} />
```

Available class mappings: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `text-background`, `bg-card`, `text-card-foreground`, `bg-primary`, `text-primary`, `text-primary-foreground`, `bg-secondary`, `text-secondary-foreground`, `bg-muted`, `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-accent`, `text-accent-foreground`, `bg-destructive`, `text-destructive-foreground`, `border-border`, `bg-border`, `bg-input`, `ring-ring`, `bg-chart`.

### `useThemeCn()` - For Custom Light/Dark Classes

Use for custom Tailwind classes not covered by `useThemeColorClassName()`:

```tsx
import { useThemeCn } from "@/lib/theme/hooks";

const tcn = useThemeCn();

<View className={tcn({ light: "bg-cyan-200", dark: "bg-cyan-700" })} />;
```

### `useTheme()` - For Theme State and Conditional Logic

Use when you need `isDark` for conditional rendering or when setting the theme:

```tsx
import { useTheme } from "@/lib/theme/context";

const { isDark, setTheme } = useTheme();

// For icon colors when useThemeColor isn't available
const iconColor = isDark ? colors.foreground.dark : colors.foreground.DEFAULT;
```

## Preference Order

1. `useThemeColorClassName()` for NativeWind classes (most common)
2. `useThemeColor()` for raw color values (icons, charts)
3. `useThemeCn()` for custom light/dark class pairs
4. `useTheme()` with `isDark` only when the above don't cover your case
